# Touchstone-86, ram_fault: D5 of the odd RAM bank stuck low: test 02 fails at case 02, a RAM word, the frame first.
# For DS1 (LO on the silk): set CONST ROLE = 1 in Touchstone.bas.
# Written by TTLSim's TouchstoneRomTests from tstrom.asm on Ida's 8086 core at 4 MHz; not edited by hand.
# Power-on at 0; the CPU leaves reset at 250 ms.
THING OledThing
0.000 B=5A
250.024 B=00
1257.406 B=FF
1262.708 B=02
1268.027 B=10
1273.345 B=22
1278.664 B=31
1283.985 B=40
1289.303 B=50
1294.622 B=60
1299.940 B=70
1305.263 B=8F
1310.581 B=9F
1315.900 B=AF
1321.218 B=BF
1326.541 B=CD
1331.859 B=DF
1337.178 B=EF
1342.496 B=FF
1347.803 B=02
END 1848.000
